# Configs reference templates

## Canonical source

`tester-v1/configs/reference/` is the only source for shared probe YAML. The create-model-configs skill copies from here, never from live model dirs.

**In reference:** global probes for calibration and manual `--server` / `--client` runs (`calibration-footprint`, `calibration-ctx-probe`, `hello-world-baseline`, plus any future promoted probes).

**Not in reference:** per-model variants such as `bench/` or one-off experiments. Add those only under `configs/{model_slug}/`.

## Promote / demote

- **Promote:** add `{variant}/server.yaml` and `client.yaml` under `reference/`, then register the variant in `model_calibration` (today hardcoded to the three names above). Do not copy probe YAML into live model dirs; see `configs-reference-sync.mdc`.
- **Demote:** remove from `reference/` only; live copies may stay.

**Default edits:** change shared behavior in `reference/`. One-off tweaks stay in that model's variant dir and are not copied to `reference/` unless promoted.

When `reference/` changes, follow `configs-reference-sync.mdc`.

## How calibration uses reference

`model_calibration.py` checks `configs/reference/{variant}/`, then runs `single_test_runner.py` with:

- `config_dir` = `configs/{model}/{variant}/` (ephemeral dir for result layout; parent supplies `model.yaml`)
- `--server` / `--client` = `configs/reference/{variant}/`

## Do not run on reference

Never pass `config_dir` under `configs/reference/` to `single_test_runner.py` or `model_calibration.py`.
